  "prefLabel": "Ch 103.03 Board Member Ethics",
  "priorExpiration": "1999-05-18",
  "recordType": "rule-section",
  "ruleText": "Ch 103.03 Board Member Ethics. No board member shall:\n\n(a) Participate in any action related to the issuance of a license or disciplinary matter involving such board member or a person with whom the board member is personally or professionally associated; and\n\n(b) Serve as an officer of a professional association which represents practitioners of any occupation or profession under the jurisdiction of the board.\n\nSource. #5624, eff 5-18-93, EXPIRED: 5-18-99\n\nNew. #7516, eff 6-27-01; ss by #14207, eff 3-7-25",
  "source": "https://github.com/GraniteState/adm-rules-data/blob/1c92d82e0f03a582ca5b7a578588edf38de2318e/raw/2026-11-15/state_agencies/ch100-500.html"
